From: Muhammad Jagot <MoJagotasdfgh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:03:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fork 002: private defaults (own keys, no install count, no
 trailers, fork update feed)

What: a new file, cmd/holyarrs/fork_defaults.go. On every start, before the
metadata mode and "Count this install" are read, it writes the settings
rows this fork keeps private when the owner has not set them: metadata
mode "own" (Your own keys: the HolyArrs metadata server is never
contacted), install_country_count off, autoplay_trailers off (so the
trailer pass stays quiet). A choice made in Settings is never overwritten.
The update check reads this fork's releases.

Why: a private home install that does not phone home by default.

Check: cmd/holyarrs/fork_check_002_test.go (fresh database gets the three
rows and mode own is in force; an owner's choice stays; main() seeds before
it reads; the update feed is the fork's).

Note: under go test the start-up seed does nothing (testing.Testing()), so
upstream's own tests keep upstream's defaults; the check tests the seed.

Upstream files edited: cmd/holyarrs/main.go, two lines changed in place
(metadata.NewHosted becomes forkHosted, which seeds first; the update feed
default); no lines added, as upstream caps main.go at 800 lines.
No database migration: ordinary settings rows.
